          "dealing": "Varies by round. Round 1: 1 card each. Round 2: 2 cards each. (Ascending up to 10 or 12, then descending back to 1).",
          "hasPlaceholders": false
        },
        "rules": {
          "objective": "Score the most points by winning EXACTLY the number of tricks you bid.",
          "gameplay": "Play starts with the player to the dealer's left leading any card. Players must follow suit if able; otherwise they may play any card including trump. Highest trump wins the trick, or if no trump was played, highest card of the led suit wins. The trick winner leads to the next trick; play continues until all tricks are complete.",
          "keyRules": [
            "Bid the exact number of tricks you will take; scoring only for making the bid exactly.",
            "Follow suit if able; if void, may play any card including trump.",
            "Trump is determined by the card turned after the deal; highest trump or highest of led suit wins the trick.",
            "The Hook: dealer may not bid so that total bids equal the number of tricks in the hand.",
            "Hand sizes follow the River: start at 10 (or 8/7 by player count), decrease to 1, then increase back."
          ],
          "hasPlaceholders": false
        },
        "strategy": {
          "basic": "In a 1-card round, if you have a high trump (Ace or King), bid 1; otherwise, bid 0. As the hand size grows, evaluate your 'Safe Tricks' (Aces/Kings in short suits) and your 'Danger Tricks' (Queens/Jacks) which might win unexpectedly.",
          "intermediate": "The 'Zero Bid' Defense: If you bid zero, your goal is to discard high cards as early as possible on other people's tricks. If you have a King and someone leads that suit, throw it on! Don't get stuck with high cards in the final tricks when you have no other choice but to win.",
          "advanced": "Social Manipulation (The Undercut): If the bids are 'Under' (total bids < tricks available), someone will be forced to win a trick they didn't want. Use this. If you bid 1 and you've already won your trick, start leading low cards in your long suits to force the opponents who wanted 0 tricks to win them.",
          "tips": [
            "If you are the dealer and the total bids are currently equal to the tricks, you ARE 'The Hooked'. You must bid something else, forcing the table into unbalanced territory.",
            "Don't bid 1 with a 'middling' card like a 7 or 8 unless it is a trump and the hand size is large."
          ],
          "hasPlaceholders": false
        },
