        "prompts": {
          "human": "Oh Hell (also known as Oh Hell!) is a classic trick-taking card game that emphasizes precision bidding over raw power. Unlike most trick-takers where you try to win as many tricks as possible, the goal is to win exactly the number of tricks you bid. It is famous for its 'River' structure, where hand sizes increase and decrease throughout the game, and its 'Hook' rule that prevents every player from being successful simultaneously.",
          "ai": "Game: Oh Hell. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay."
        },
        "scoring": {
          "description": "10 points bonus for making your bid + 1 point per trick taken. If you miss your bid, you get 0 points (or 1 point per trick with no bonus).",
